# An uncovered dictionary whose subject is an APPLIED CONSTRUCTOR, not a bare
# type variable.
#
# `try_map` generalizes `e` and its body needs `Applicative (Result e)`. The
# diagnostic used to name the bare variable — "for type variable `e`" — and suggest
# `where Applicative e`, which cannot be right: `e` is the error type (String,
# PgError), not the applicative. Following that suggestion moved the error to the
# CALL site as "No instance of Applicative for String", a worse place to work the
# answer out from.
#
# The constraint the reader must write is on the partially applied constructor; only
# the advice was wrong. run/dispatch_compound_head_partial_ctor.spr compiles and runs
# the advised form.
module main

fn try_map(f: a -> Result e b, xs: List a) -> Result e (List b) =
  traverse(f, xs)

fn main() -> Unit !{IO} = print("x")
